absolute minimum.

26
00:01:50,022 --> 00:01:53,392
They occur either at critical points or at
the endpoints.

27
00:01:54,533 --> 00:01:59,738
A critical point is where f prime equals
zero or f prime does not exist.

28
00:02:00,188 --> 00:02:05,628
Every local max or min of a differentiable
function happens at a critical point.

29
00:02:06,766 --> 00:02:11,576
The closed interval method: find the
critical points inside the interval,

30
00:02:11,576 --> 00:02:14,937
evaluate f there and at the endpoints, and
compare.

31
00:02:15,387 --> 00:02:18,736
The biggest value is the max; the smallest
is the min.

32
00:02:19,866 --> 00:02:26,224
Find the extremes of f of x equals x cubed
minus three x on negative two to three.

33
00:02:26,674 --> 00:02:32,783
f prime is three x squared minus three,
zero at plus or minus one. f of negative

34
00:02:32,783 --> 00:02:39,122
two is negative two, f of negative one is
two, f of one is negative two, f of three

35
00:02:39,122 --> 00:02:42,482
