50
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:43,755
The first derivative test: if f prime
changes from positive to negative at c, f

51
00:03:43,755 --> 00:03:48,431
has a local max at c. From negative to
positive, a local min.

52
00:03:48,881 --> 00:03:51,163
No sign change means no extremum.

53
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:58,679
f of x equals x to the fourth minus four x
cubed. f prime is four x cubed minus

54
00:03:58,679 --> 00:04:03,201
twelve x squared, or four x squared times
x minus three.

55
00:04:03,651 --> 00:04:09,534
Critical points zero and three. f prime is
negative, negative, positive. So no

56
00:04:09,534 --> 00:04:15,342
